// P0 overlay on top of @platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl (Renode 1.17.0).
// Each entry: the symptom seen in Renode, the cause, and the RM0433 reference.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DBGMCU (RM0433, debug chapter: DBGMCU_IDC identity code register, 0x5C001000;
//         CMSIS: DBGMCU->IDCODE in stm32h743xx.h)
// Symptom: "ReadDoubleWord from non existing peripheral at 0x5C001000" followed by
//          "WriteDoubleWord to ... 0x51008108 (tag GPV_matrix_(AXIM))".
// Cause:   DBGMCU isn't modeled, so IDCODE reads 0. SystemInit()
//          (Core/Src/system_stm32h7xx.c:262) treats REV_ID < 0x2000 as silicon
//          revision Y and applies the rev-Y AXI switch-matrix errata write.
//          The NUCLEO-H743ZI2 is revision V (REV_ID 0x2003), which skips it,
//          so the emulated boot path differed from the real board.
// Fix:     report the board's identity: REV_ID 0x2003 (rev V), DEV_ID 0x450.
//          Reserved bits 15:12 are left 0 (HAL only uses 31:16 and 11:0).
//          Python peripheral = prototype per .claude/rules/renode.md; it is
//          read-only identity data, so there is nothing to grow into C# yet.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dbgmcu: Python.PythonPeripheral @ sysbus 0x5C001000
    size: 0x400
    initable: false
    script: '''
if request.Offset == 0x00: # IDCODE
    request.Value = 0x20030450
else:
    request.Value = 0
'''
